EvalSuite[skillName=returns-and-recall-management, evals=[Eval[id=1, prompt=A customer requests a return for Product SKU-992 (a controlled pharmaceutical) citing 'damaged packaging' 10 days after delivery. The original order was confirmed delivered. The system currently has the return status as 'Pending'. What actions should be taken regarding authorization and routing?, expectedOutput=The system must NOT auto-authorize the return. It must flag the item as a controlled product requiring regulatory review and route it to the Regulatory Review team. It must also note that because the reason is quality-related, QA approval is additionally required before physical collection is arranged., files=[], expectations=[Must explicitly state that automatic authorization is prohibited for controlled products., Must identify that Regulatory Review is required due to the controlled product status., Must identify that QA approval is required due to the quality-related return reason., Must not generate a Return Authorization (RA) number until both regulatory and QA reviews are complete.]], Eval[id=2, prompt=A batch of returned goods (Batch ID: RET-2023-004) has arrived at the warehouse dock. The driver claims the goods are 'good condition' and asks to put them away in the main storage area to save time. The QA team has not yet inspected them. What is the correct procedure?, expectedOutput=The system must reject the request to put goods away. The goods must be physically and systemically moved to QUARANTINE status. No movement to saleable inventory is permitted until QA completes an assessment and issues a disposition (Release, Return to Manufacturer, Destroy, or Continue Quarantine)., files=[], expectations=[Must explicitly prohibit moving returned goods directly to saleable/main inventory., Must mandate that the inventory status be set to QUARANTINE immediately upon receipt., Must state that QA assessment is a mandatory prerequisite for any disposition decision., Must not allow the driver's verbal claim of 'good condition' to override the quarantine protocol.]], Eval[id=3, prompt=A regulatory recall notice is issued for Batch ID: BATCH-XYZ-123. The system shows 500 units in Warehouse A, 50 units in transit to Customer B, and 100 units delivered to Customer C. What immediate containment actions must be triggered?, expectedOutput=The system must block allocation of Batch ID: BATCH-XYZ-123 in Warehouse A, suspend picking for this batch, and quarantine the 500 units. It must attempt to intercept the 50 in-transit units. It must generate customer notifications for Customer C regarding the 100 delivered units. Normal operations for this batch must be halted., files=[], expectations=[Must trigger a block on allocation and picking for the specific batch ID., Must set the status of the 500 warehouse units to QUARANTINE., Must initiate an interception workflow for the 50 in-transit units., Must generate customer notification tasks for the delivered units., Must prioritize these actions over any pending normal order processing for this SKU.]], Eval[id=4, prompt=The Compliance Team is attempting to close Recall ID: REC-2024-001. The total recalled quantity is 1,000 units. The current reconciliation shows: 400 held in warehouse, 100 in transit (intercepted), 300 delivered, 150 returned, and 50 destroyed. The sum is 1,000. Can the recall be closed?, expectedOutput=No, the recall cannot be closed yet. While the quantities sum to the total, the system must verify that all 'held' and 'in-transit' units are physically accounted for and that the 'returned' units have completed QA disposition. Furthermore, the Compliance Team must explicitly approve the closure after verifying that no unexplained quantities exist (e.g., ensuring the 150 returned units are not just 'received' but fully processed/disposed). The prompt implies a check for 'unexplained quantities' which usually requires detailed audit trails, not just a sum check., files=[], expectations=[Must state that the recall cannot be closed solely based on the arithmetic sum matching the total., Must require verification that all 'held' and 'in-transit' units are physically secured/quarantined., Must require that 'returned' units have a final disposition status (not just 'received')., Must require explicit approval from the Compliance Team for final closure., Must flag that 'unexplained quantities' must be resolved, implying a need for audit trail verification beyond simple counting.]]]]